<Base title="About" section="about" description="A railway reservation terminal, a QBASIC app in fourth class, and how I ended up writing software for a living.">
  <header class="page-title">
    <h1>About</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="prose article-body">
    <p>I was in fourth class when I saw a computer running a terminal application at a railway station. I’d gone to get tickets booked and was mesmerised. A person books a ticket here, and that seat gets locked across the entire railway network.</p>
    <p>The next week I was introduced to QBASIC and naively tried to create my own reservation app. It worked, though there was no storage or persistence, just a simple read-write application. A glorified hello world, basically. I haven’t felt that same sense of achievement since XD</p>

    <h2>These days</h2>
    <p>I’m from Sagar in Madhya Pradesh and now live in Bangalore, where I write software for a living. I’ve been doing that since 2020. These days I lead the Integrations team at <a href="/work/#regie">Regie.ai</a>.</p>
    <p>Leading a team is extremely difficult. I’m learning things about myself haha. I care a lot about people using their own brains and taking ownership of what they build, and I’m figuring out how to help that happen. We’re also on a tight timeline to deliver a new product, so my priorities are a bit fucked up right now.</p>

    <h2>Movies</h2>
    <p>I love reading about directors and then watching their movies. Gives me a whole new perspective. Recently I watched Shoojit Sircar’s interview with Samdish and really liked how calm he was, how clearly he thought about things. You can see that in <em>Piku</em>. The story flows so naturally, but there’s so much attention to detail in the scenes and characters.</p>
    <p>I wanted a place of my own to share <a href="/thoughts/">what I’m learning</a> and the things I build. That’s why this site exists. Movies will probably find their way in too.</p>
    <p>If there’s a director you think I should watch, <a href="mailto:hi@ajay.guru">send me a film to start with</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
